    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0437" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-26T15:00:00+01:00">March 26, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2459. For Assistant Secretary Berle. Department’s 2286, March 25. Thank you for
                    forwarding me your schedule. I believe it is well thought out and the time
                    allotted ample to carry out your program.</p>
                <p>I think your stopover in Canada was a wise and constructive method of handling a
                    difficult situation.</p>
                <p>I have already explained to Satterthwaite that he is to be attached to you on
                    your arrival.</p>
                <p>. . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
